# Architecture (DDD)

Follow Domain-Driven Design. Keep layers separated; do not mix UI, domain, and infrastructure.

## Layers

```
src/
  domain/          # entities, value objects, domain types, business rules
  application/     # use cases, app services, ports (interfaces)
  infrastructure/  # API clients, storage, adapters implementing ports
  presentation/    # pages, widgets, features UI, hooks tied to UI
  shared/          # cross-cutting utils, i18n, config (no business logic)
```

## Rules

- Domain has **no** imports from React, HeroUI, axios, or router
- Application orchestrates use cases; depends on domain + ports only
- Infrastructure implements ports (axios, localStorage, etc.)
- Presentation calls application use cases / stores; no direct axios in components
- Feature folders map to bounded contexts (e.g. `categories`, `products`, `auth`)
- Prefer explicit types and value objects over raw strings/numbers for domain concepts

## ❌ BAD

```ts
// presentation calling axios directly
const { data } = await axios.get('/categories')
```

## ✅ GOOD

```ts
// presentation → application use case → infrastructure adapter
await categoriesService.list()
```
